From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lvgl: compact pending invalid areas covered by newer regions

The invalid-area queue contains only 32 entries.  LVGL already drops a new
area when an older pending area covers it, but it keeps older child areas when
a newer parent area covers them.  A burst of child updates can therefore fill
the queue and fall back to a full-screen redraw before refresh-time joining.

Compact fully covered older entries when the newer area is collected.  This
does not change the visible dirty union; it only represents that union with
fewer queue entries earlier in the refresh pipeline.

---
 src/core/lv_refr.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/lv_refr.c b/src/core/lv_refr.c
--- a/src/core/lv_refr.c
+++ b/src/core/lv_refr.c
@@ -247,6 +247,24 @@ void _lv_inv_area(lv_disp_t * disp, const lv_area_t * area_p)
         if(_lv_area_is_in(&com_area, &disp->inv_areas[i], 0) != false) return;
     }
 
+    /*If the new area covers older pending areas, remove the older entries
+     *immediately.  Keeping both until lv_refr_join_area() wastes slots in the
+     *small invalid-area queue and can make a burst of child invalidations
+     *overflow to a full-screen redraw before their parent is invalidated.*/
+    uint16_t kept = 0;
+    for(i = 0; i < disp->inv_p; i++) {
+        if(_lv_area_is_in(&disp->inv_areas[i], &com_area, 0) != false) {
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        if(kept != i) {
+            lv_area_copy(&disp->inv_areas[kept], &disp->inv_areas[i]);
+        }
+        disp->inv_area_joined[kept] = 0;
+        kept++;
+    }
+    disp->inv_p = kept;
+
     /*Save the area*/
     if(disp->inv_p < LV_INV_BUF_SIZE) {
         lv_area_copy(&disp->inv_areas[disp->inv_p], &com_area);
-- 
